      "id": "claim_90d3031488b246f3931cda210aaddde1",
      "statement": "The two production MongoDB stores have deliberately different auth shapes: `mc-service-store-mongo` is a single-member replica set (`rs0`) and therefore needs a replica-set keyfile, which implies `--auth`, plus SCRAM users, while `mcm-bff-store-mongo` is standalone and needs SCRAM credentials only and never a keyfile.",
