    {
      "id": "claim_8475f41579c84c3ab9a8dd2b334833c2",
      "statement": "There is no image-revert rollback for the 9.0 upgrade: MongoDB supports a binary downgrade from 9.0 only to the latest 8.0 patch, never to 8.0.8, and the volume has been re-owned to uid 1000, so rollback is a dump restored onto a fresh 8.0.8 volume — a path rehearsed both from the pre-flight archive and from a dump taken on 9.0 at FCV 9.0.",
