      "id": "claim_0807fb1eb11e4f02a4b750e1391eea67",
      "statement": "9.0-ubi9 runs mongod as uid 1000 where 8.0.8-ubi9 ran it as uid 998, so an 8.0.8-written volume is foreign-owned and 9.0 dies at start with `Unable to read the storage engine metadata file ... storage.bson` (`FileNotOpen`); therefore every MongoDB service mounting `/data/db` starts as `user: \"0:0\"` only to re-own the directory once and then drops to the image's `mongod` user with `setpriv`, and mongod itself never runs as root.",
