      "statement": "The keyfile permission check is defense-in-depth rather than incidental: `mongod` refuses to start on a group- or world-readable keyfile, and because the entrypoint re-materializes it at 0400 on every clean start, a manually widened keyfile self-heals on the next redeploy instead of needing manual repair.",
